{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 14756306319931883011, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 616, "mtime": 1791872335.7839787, "sha256": "0b56caefa48d9b6110d66d889838af8f9f541dfdc5881a4914cb618bcdd16753"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 328, "mtime": 1791872335.787979, "sha256": "ed9f7eacd479df6461cadbd1e0ff105a27d0092a4c0a9b468aad0cbc82453133"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/23/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/23/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Fixed. `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** `round(x, 2)` worked on the binary float. 2.675 is actually stored as 2.67499999\u2026, so it rounded down. `round()` also uses banker's rounding (ties go to the even digit), so even exact ties like `0.125` came out as `0.12`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the float into a `Decimal` using its shortest decimal form, `repr(x)` (so `\"2.675\"`), rounds to cents half up, and returns a `float` as before. `add_vat` calls `round_money`, so it picks up the fix too.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`:\n- The new regression test `tests/test_round_money.py` passes. It checks `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68` and `2.674\u21922.67`.\n- The existing `test_split` still passes.\n- Plain `round(2.675, 2)` still gives `2.67`, which confirms the old bug.\n\nThere's no git repo here, so I couldn't stash the fix to watch the new test fail against the old code. That `round()` check shows it would fail.\n\nNegative halves round away from zero (`-2.675\u2192-2.68`).\n\n**Not fixed:** `split()` has a similar float problem. `int(total * 100)` cuts off the decimals instead of rounding, so `0.29 * 100` becomes `28.999\u2026` and then `28`. I didn't change it because it wasn't part of this request.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 224791, "requests_cache_write": 6754, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1192002, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2020, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial23", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null,